{"title":"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 41","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_41&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A girls' camp is located <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b899aba26cc33f0026125daebb44a60349c999b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> rods from a straight road. On this road, a boys' camp is located <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a39b14023c98c943554d150561aacc188c4ce26d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> rods from the girls' camp. \nIt is desired to build a canteen on the road which shall be exactly the same distance from each camp. \nThe distance of the canteen from each of the camps is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/b/8fbabcef91187b6285b9cdd0aa1ba57b4824e164.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 400\\text{ rods} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 250\\text{ rods} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 87.5\\text{ rods} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 200\\text{ rods}\\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"497\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_41&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/3/88300a9a628eefa1c829cff1fe473477346e7af4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(6,0)); draw((1,0)--(1,3)--(5,0)); draw((1,3)--(1.875,0)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(1,0),S); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(5,0),S); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(1.875,0),S); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,(1,3),NW); label(&quot;$r$&quot;,(0,0),SW); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"162\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the straight road, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the girls' camp, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the boys' camp, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the water canteen. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f0f6aa257bd96696d97454bb777b1a283069e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AG}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> is the perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Suppose each rod is one unit long. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b89b95c05d90c639bacc0d400b12d2cca43655e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG=300$\" width=\"78\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/3/be3e53fbc3e78cf3d2f5aa5ddb22834004bd590b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BG=500$\" width=\"79\" height=\"12\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/2/cf2d89adc05fd45e58fac3d0b4513cd98b124555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle GAB$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> is a right angle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/d/b3d7aade27b35f9df070273a73a017d9c8877db8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle GAB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/1/af1a2cb4ff1720f169ddde1726c1a5a1ab816ae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3-4-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" /> right triangle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31cccd17042022533ad2b1c4333f5080226c371d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=400$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the distance from the canteen to the girls' and boys' camps. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/7/0b7937f9664c22dc4dbc6ac1733ca5d1ac729c53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=CG=x$\" width=\"116\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3be6fdc0cb72c0421d0357ca835a0b2f1907274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=400-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"111\" height=\"13\" />. Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/9/e694f2d1ee2424a0161eaccdd943b86666fa662b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle GAC$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/c/98c73b7e61f4cb3ffd8ebcfe6c49578faa688c17.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[300^2+(400-x)^2=x^2\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"19\" /> \nSimplifying the left side gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3928de506b539905801d3437b8cd15101eb14c42.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[90000+160000-800x+x^2=x^2\\]\" width=\"262\" height=\"16\" />\nSubtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> from both sides and rearranging gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72290b63b4fa147d365645d37cd486afd3b194fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[800x=250000\\]\" width=\"115\" height=\"12\" />\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e29be9aaa5efc394256bec4a888dad84039b0c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{250000}{800}=312.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"158\" height=\"37\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/f/77f02753f9a328103e8713e63ba165e4d8e2d432.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"140\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_41&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2e3821cf99757d18251a531926677bbd2bac827.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(6,0)); draw((1,0)--(1,3)--(5,0)); draw((1,3)--(1.875,0)); draw((1.875,0)--(3,1.5)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(1,0),S); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(5,0),S); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(1.875,0),S); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,(1,3),NW); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,(3,1.5),NE); label(&quot;$r$&quot;,(0,0),SW); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"162\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the road, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the girls' camp, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the boys' camp, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the water canteen, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a69cff9810d26c7644f654be37b82c10323bc055.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BG}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/8/9f8264fdf9eae459b910b43ca74f1c300d4945fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BG = 500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/143b3edf8008ea2d4eb39ddb0be5ad255e7424f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG = 300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />, by the Pythagorean theorem <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/8/1e8031b1e44f3920143909fd024e9f9bc131e3de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = \\sqrt{500^2-300^2}=400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"213\" height=\"21\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a69cff9810d26c7644f654be37b82c10323bc055.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BG}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4ad5e119db95e127c7644801bd794f74be51bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MB = 250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"14\" />.  Also, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/4/7746dedcc184722d984662d10af1978737cb8d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle GCB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is isosceles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/349e0f4a1538fbf6cf43300e81736691db9acee0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CMB$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" /> is a right angle.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/9/d791b6ca78f49b28d8ac595b1322bb8a8cd1d344.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle GAB \\sim \\triangle CMB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/2/742014068e78a959dc6d7d635c7cf5d64c2aabb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{MB}{BC} = \\frac{AB}{BG}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"39\" />, that is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/4/ba44fb21f4d628916521d3e1c5ab462741b0c2ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{250}{BC} = \\frac{400}{500}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" />. Solving yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/4/3049631a4f01c4574f529e5a8affb24d17fb2fd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 312.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"14\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/f/77f02753f9a328103e8713e63ba165e4d8e2d432.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"140\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_41&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME\" title=\"1953 AHSME\">1953 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1953 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1953\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_40\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 40\">Problem 40</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_42\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 42\">Problem 42</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title